  nonce: '4576'  # 4576
  data:  # 4576
    kind: work_item  # 4576
    title: "node.id NAME slot disagrees with node.name on 255 synthetic nodes (linker category constant / route method+path stuffed into {name} slot per spec §317)"  # 4576
    status: todo_hard  # 4576
    priority: 2  # 4576
    parent:  # 4576
    tags:  # 4576
    - dogfood  # 4576
    - dogfood_tranche_05  # 4576
    isbefore: []  # 4576
    duplicate_of: []  # 4576
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 4576
    pr_ref:  # 4576
    description: "Spec §317 defines node id as {lang}:{file}:{span}:{name}:{kind} — the second-from-last colon segment is {name}. On 255 synthetic nodes the id name slot carries a GENERIC linker-category constant (or a method+path route label) while node.name carries the SPECIFIC value, so a consumer reconstructing a node's name by parsing its documented stable id gets a different string than node.name. 255 non-file id-name mismatches: 130 call_site + 124 function + 1 method. Linker nodes use a category constant in the id name slot vs specific node.name: subprocess_call(78)->name 'git config'/'ls'; db_query(34)->name 'SELECT users'/'DELETE items'; mq_publisher(44)/mq_subscriber(31)->name 'kafka:publish:topic'; http_client(18)->name 'GET /api/users'; resolver(11)->name 'Query.users'/'Mutation.createUser'; WS endpoint functions id '/ws-endpoint'->name 'ws:/ws'. Starlette route-registration nodes: id name slot is METHOD+PATH ('GET /health','POST /api/items') while node.name is 'starlette:_health' (framework+handler form). Rust separator case: id 'MyStruct.method' vs node.name 'MyStruct::method'. Fresh repro: hypergumbo run on /tmp/hg_nameslot/runner.py (two subprocess.run calls) -> python:runner.py:4-4:subprocess_call:call_site name='git config' MISMATCH. Consequence: an agent indexing nodes by parsed-id-name collapses all 78 subprocess call_sites under 'subprocess_call', all 34 db queries under 'db_query', etc., even though node.name distinguishes them."  # 4576
    fields: {}  # 4576
